  "original_report_text": "1308 trim revision002 visual review — PASS\n\nThe original split/streak blocker is resolved. Across three matched native stills and all nine new original AVI samples, the pale gable fascia reads as one solid band. In particular, 68/113/143 no longer show the long broken secondary streak observed before. Small localized ridge joints do not reproduce that defect. Selected pad/post junctions and representative-front proportions remain coherent; no further visual correction is required for this delta.\n\nVerified all 243 current pins, native/motion pre/post bindings and clean terminal logs, durable copies, and all nine payloads against the original AVI. Camera positions and lights match the originals exactly; 03/04 forwards also match. The literal-vector check found that 06 forward Y differs by 1.9371509552e-7 despite the helper’s rounded zero-angle result. Its orientation match is tolerance-level, with no observed visual consequence. Source/collision preservation remains separate technical evidence. The earlier HOLD and failed external acosf capture remain immutable history.\n\nFrame 158 visibly retains the world; 159–161 payloads match it exactly. The held PNG is bound but not independently replayed; original 162 remains retained teardown evidence. The 163-frame 1280×800 AVI is 15,811,474 bytes; its RIFF declaration ends at 15,811,404, 70 bytes before physical EOF within the trailing index. No continuous playback, generic-player compatibility, absent-intervening-flicker or exact encoded/physics/process alignment claim is made.\n\nThis PASS covers the changed trim finish in current 11/213 live context. It does not turn obstructed historical whole views into usable proof, replay unrelated art, certify mechanics or grant credit/package acceptance. No engine or product edit was performed. Exact bindings and named RETRO are in [REVIEW.json](REVIEW.json).\n",
